{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered while fixing bug regardable-superduper-whiteeye (dca1-f641-caeb-4df4), which fixed ONE\ntest. This covers the rest of the class, surveyed but left out of that change.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nA fixture creates a bare git repo with a raw `git init --bare` and pushes into it. At git's\ndefaults a bare repo's `receive-pack` runs `run_auto_maintenance()` after every push, spawning\n`git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` — a process that OUTLIVES the push. So\n`subprocess.run([... \"push\" ...])` returning is NOT a happens-before edge for that object database.\nIf the test then COPIES or byte-walks that directory it races a concurrent repack: entries vanish\nmid-walk and the copy raises. Measured signatures: a vanished `objects/maintenance.lock` (what CI\ncaught) and whole loose-object fanout directories (`objects/2c`, ...) pruned as maintenance packs\nthem.\n\nrebar pins the two `autoDetach` keys on every store it OWNS (`_commands/_init_ensures.py`; bug\n88eb, ADR 0051). A fixture-built bare remote is owned by no rebar code, so it runs at defaults.\nThat asymmetry is the gap.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe remedy is settled and measured — pin `gc.autoDetach=false`, `maintenance.autoDetach=false`,\n`receive.autogc=false` on the bare repo immediately after creating it, before anything is pushed.\nMeasured postures, each with `receive-pack` confirmed present in a `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` trace:\ndefaults -> 1 detached child; autoDetach pins only -> 1 foreground child; all three -> 0 children.\nStructural, not probabilistic. Three steps:\n\n1. **One shared definition.** A new `tests/_git_upkeep.py` owns the pins\n   (`BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS`), the constructor applying them (`init_bare_remote`), and the trace\n   helpers proving their effect (`maintenance_children`, `assert_no_detached_upkeep`), following the\n   small single-purpose `tests/_*.py` convention (`_git_counts.py`, `_subprocess_env.py`).\n   `test_concurrency_regression.py` and `test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` hold byte-identical copies of\n   those keys under two names today; both are repointed at the helper, ending that drift.\n\n2. **Fix the two HIGH-risk sites** by routing their bare-repo creation through that helper.\n\n3. **Close the class at the amplifier.** `clone_topology_template` (`tests/_topology_template.py`)\n   is the only mechanism in `tests/` copying a whole topology containing a bare remote — a\n   `shutil.copytree(...)` plus two full-tree `rglob(\"*\")` + `read_bytes()` passes. It gains a\n   precondition REFUSING a template that holds an unpinned bare repository, naming the path and the\n   missing keys, so a future fixture reintroducing the pattern fails loudly at setup instead of\n   flaking under a race.\n\nNOT acceptable, per dca1: retrying the copy, sleeping before it, or excluding `*.lock` from the\nwalk — that filter is measurably insufficient, since the repack limb prunes whole fanout\ndirectories, not just lock files.\n\n## The two HIGH-risk sites (push, then the tree holding the bare repo is copied)\n\n1. `test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` — raw `init -q --bare` in `_build_backup_fixture`, pushing\n   immediately after (`push --all`, `push --tags`); the topology is copied via\n   `clone_topology_template` once per test in the module. No pins in the file.\n2. `test_inline_write_push.py` — raw `init -q --bare` in `_build_repo_with_origin`;\n   `rebar.init_repo(...)` pushes under the default `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`; copied via\n   `clone_topology_template`. No pins.\n\n## The MEDIUM sites: bounded by the amplifier, not swept\n\nThe survey counted ~35 further sites pushing into an unpinned bare repo. They are NOT swept here,\non a measured exposure predicate: a site is exposed only when the bare remote lives inside a tree\nlater copied or byte-walked, and `clone_topology_template` is the only thing in `tests/` doing that\nto a whole topology. It has seven callers — two are the HIGH sites above, one is the already-pinned\n`test_concurrency_regression.py`, one is the module itself, and the remaining three\n(`tests/interfaces/_store_template.py`, `tests/interfaces/queries/test_list_filters.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py`) create no bare repository at all. Every other site pushes\ninto a bare repo nothing copies, so there is no walk to race.\n\nSweeping three keys across ~35 unaffected files would be a large unreviewable diff whose bulk is\nunnecessary. Step 3 replaces that sweep with an enforced precondition: the moment any such site\nacquires a copy step, the guard converts a latent flake into a deterministic setup failure naming\nthe fix. The exposed set closes by construction, not by an enumeration that decays.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py` (new) — the pins, the pinned constructor, the trace proof helpers.\n- `tests/_topology_template.py` — the unpinned-bare-repo precondition on `clone_topology_template`.\n- `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` — drop its local pins, use the helper.\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` — drop its pins and trace reader, use the helper.\n- `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` — HIGH site: build through the helper, guard.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py` — HIGH site: build through the helper, guard.\n- `tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py` (new) — cover the precondition both ways.\n\nStacked on Gerrit 1952 (the dca1 fix, `Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1`, unsubmitted), which\nintroduces the second copy of the pins that step 1 collapses.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a push into each newly-pinned remote leaves no detached upkeep, asserted from git's\n  own `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` trace, behind a `receive-pack` positive control so it cannot pass against\n  an empty trace.\n- Failure path: `clone_topology_template` raises `AssertionError` naming the unpinned bare repo and\n  the missing keys when handed such a template, and returns normally once it is pinned.\n- Discrimination: per changed site, seed the defect its test guards, observe RED on the expected\n  assertion, revert, observe GREEN; separately empty the pins and watch the trace guard fire.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/` holds exactly one assignment site for the upkeep pins, `tests/_git_upkeep.py`;\n      checked by `[ \"$(grep -rl 'receive.autogc' tests/ | wc -l)\" -eq 1 ]`.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` consumes the shared definition instead of\n      its own copy; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` consumes the shared definition instead of its\n      own copy; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` creates its bare remote with the pins\n      applied before its first push; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py` creates its bare remote with the pins\n      applied before its first push; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] A push into each newly-pinned remote leaves no detached upkeep; checked by a test per site\n      running the push under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT`, asserting no `git maintenance run` child carries\n      `--detach`, with a `receive-pack` positive control against a vacuous pass.\n- [ ] `clone_topology_template` refuses a template holding an unpinned bare repository, and accepts\n      that same template once pinned; checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py -q`.\n- [ ] Each newly-pinned site's guard discriminates; checked by seeding the defect it guards,\n      observing RED on the expected assertion, reverting, observing GREEN.\n- [ ] The touched modules are green; checked by `pytest -q\n      tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py\n      tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py\n      tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py`.\n- [ ] The repo gates pass; checked by `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787210235644621001,"uuid":"2d4f5d4f-58a9-486c-a706-f2a949cbe653"}